 "text": "Hi, how have you been? The easiest way is to put it in the fridge. A cooler with ice and some kind of insulation, like a blanket, will keep food cold for days. Ice cubes work best, but blocks are fine if you' short on them. Just make sure they stay covered, so the ice melts slowly. Bring a few extra blankets and towels, in case the cooler gets wet or sweaty. Give him his own cooler for the weekend. Use a big bin liner inside, so it' one big bag he can't handle. Yes, train it to the cooler. Pour warm water into a cup and put the cooler next. As the water cools, the cup gets heavier, and you can see the effect.",
